## 2. `Jadens-Nether-Expansion`: The 5-Commit `Claude Opus 4.8` Code-Laundering Sequence

Target file: `src/main/java/net/jadenxgamer/netherexp/core/block/entity/PetrifiedSwirlsBlockEntity.java` on branch `1.21.1`.

### 2.1 Chronological Commit Chain

1. **`3d6606a1a784da16059fe2c1814887fb61f46c23`** (`2026-06-01 08:50:03Z`, author `ThatJadenXgamer <[redacted-private-email]>`, subject: `a lot of stuff I just forgot to commit`, `2,021` insertions):
   * Commits `PetrifiedSwirlsBlockEntity.java` containing two non-ASCII `U+2013` (`0xE2 0x80 0x93`) en-dash comments (`lines 128, 137`) and an unguarded `@OnlyIn(Dist.CLIENT)` call inside `triggerEvent(int id, int type)` that crashes dedicated servers via NeoForge `RuntimeDistCleaner`.
2. **`35da7059144e6fa662b2e63f6ae96400589540c8`** (`2026-06-03 14:53:56Z` / `20:23:56 +0530`, author `Ethan White <42824671+n0es@users.noreply.github.com>`, committer `GitHub <[redacted-private-email]> +0530`, **PGP-signed**):
   * `ThatJadenXgamer` squash-merges Pull Request `#283` through the GitHub web interface (`+0530` committer offset). The commit message contains the explicit trailer `Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
   * Refactors `triggerEvent` from 3 braced multi-line `case` blocks into 3 single-line arrow statements nested inside `if (this.level.isClientSide())`, keeping `return true;` outside the client check so `ServerLevel#doBlockEvent` still relays `ClientboundBlockEventPacket` to clients. Remains live on `1.21.1` for `27` days.
3. **`966c08d65e5e9176039e7807082824ab0b7e4579`** (`2026-06-30 10:30:29Z` / `16:00:29 +0530`, author `JadenXgamer <114387521+ThatJadenXgamer@users.noreply.github.com>`, **PGP-signed**):
   * Reverts `35da7059144e6fa662b2e63f6ae96400589540c8` via Pull Request `#294`.
   * PR `#294` body by `ThatJadenXgamer`:
     ```text
     It has come to attention that the following PR was AI generated using Claude
     and as such is being reverted. I do not condone nor support generative AI use in my personal projects, everything about JNE is 100% human made and I intend on keeping it that way.
     ```
4. **`7d77fb1a2562474f4a72950110be29d68bf3c455`** (`2026-06-30 10:36:28Z`, **`359` seconds after `966c08d65e`**, `parent: 966c08d65e5e9176039e7807082824ab0b7e4579`, author `ThatJadenXgamer <[redacted-private-email]>`, subject: `Fix Petrified Soul Swirls Server Crash`):
   * Re-commits the single-line arrow `switch` + trailing `return true;` structure from `35da705914` under `ThatJadenXgamer`'s authorship, deleting the 5-line comment from `35da705914` and moving `this.level.isClientSide()` into the outer `if` condition.
   * Because `ServerLevel#runBlockEvents` calls `triggerEvent` server-side first and only broadcasts `ClientboundBlockEventPacket` when `triggerEvent` returns `true`, moving `isClientSide()` to the outer `if` caused server calls to fall through to `super.triggerEvent()` (`false`), breaking Petrified Swirls particles in both singleplayer and multiplayer.
   * `166` seconds later (`2026-06-30 10:39:14Z`), `ThatJadenXgamer` posts on PR `#283`: `"This PR has been reverted due to the use of generative AI"`.
5. **`9dcac09339b6e7af7067b581fbc80c365de121a8`** (`2026-07-15 14:16:33Z`, `15` days later, author `ThatJadenXgamer <[redacted-private-email]>`, subject: `car ass`, `+1,369 / -37` across repo):
   * Restores the exact nested `if (this.level.isClientSide()) { switch (type) { ... } } return true;` control flow authored by `Claude Opus 4.8` in `35da705914`, omitting the explanatory comment and `n0es` / `Claude Opus 4.8` attribution.

### 2.2 Exact Code Comparison Across Commits

```java
// [A] Pre-#283 (3d6606a1a7, 2026-06-01, ThatJadenXgamer):
if (this.level != null && id == 1) {
    switch (type) {
        case 0 -> {
            PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.petrificationParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            return true;
        }
        case 1 -> {
            PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.unpetrifyParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            return true;
        }
        case 2 -> {
            PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.attractToPetrifierParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            return true;
        }
    }
}

// [B] PR #283 (35da705914, 2026-06-03, n0es + Claude Opus 4.8):
if (this.level != null && id == 1 && type >= 0 && type <= 2) {
    // The particle helpers live in PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client, which is @OnlyIn(Dist.CLIENT).
    // triggerEvent is dispatched on the server too (ServerLevel#blockEvent -> doBlockEvent),
    // so touching that class server-side trips RuntimeDistCleaner and crashes dedicated servers.
    // Only spawn particles on the client; on the server just acknowledge the event (return true)
    // so it is still relayed to nearby clients.
    if (this.level.isClientSide()) {
        switch (type) {
            case 0 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.petrificationParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            case 1 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.unpetrifyParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            case 2 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.attractToPetrifierParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
        }
    }
    return true;
}

// [C] +359s Post-Revert Rewrite (7d77fb1a25, 2026-06-30 10:36:28Z, ThatJadenXgamer - breaks server relay):
if (this.level != null && this.level.isClientSide() && id == 1) {
    switch (type) {
        case 0 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.petrificationParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
        case 1 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.unpetrifyParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
        case 2 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.attractToPetrifierParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
    }
    return true;
}

// [D] Commit "car ass" (9dcac09339, 2026-07-15, ThatJadenXgamer - live on 1.21.1 HEAD):
if (this.level != null && id == 1) {
    if (this.level.isClientSide()) {
        switch (type) {
            case 0 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.petrificationParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            case 1 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.unpetrifyParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
            case 2 -> PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client.attractToPetrifierParticle(level, level.random, getBlockPos());
        }
    }
    return true;
}
