Fix dedicated server crash from PetrifiedSwirlsBlockEntity#triggerEvent (#283)

triggerEvent unconditionally called PetrifiedSwirlsBlock.Client particle
helpers, which live in an @OnlyIn(Dist.CLIENT) class. Because block events
are dispatched server-side too (ServerLevel#blockEvent -> doBlockEvent),
this tripped NeoForge's RuntimeDistCleaner and crashed dedicated servers
whenever a Petrified Swirls block ticked its event.

Guard the particle calls behind level.isClientSide(); on the server simply
return true so the event is still relayed to clients. Same pattern used to
resolve the earlier ParticleRenderType dist crash (#269).

Fixes #282

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

