## 3. `Gleam`: `Low-Drag-MC/Shimmer` (`MIT`) License Breach, Variable Scrubbing, and OpenGL 4.3 Defects

### 3.1 `Low-Drag-MC/Shimmer` (`MIT`) License Violation

1. **Upstream License (`https://github.com/Low-Drag-MC/Shimmer`, branch `1.20`, file `LICENSE`):**
   ```text
   MIT License
   Copyright (c) 2022 Low-Drag-MC
   ...
   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
   copies or substantial portions of the Software.
   ```
2. **Written Admission of Derivation (`ThatJadenXgamer/Gleam`, `README.md` line `137`, added in `2bb5dd5`):**
   ```text
   **[Shimmer](https://modrinth.com/mod/shimmer!)** - A small chunk of Gleam's colored lights code was derived from Shimmer's as a starting-off point, which I've since iterated on and changed quite drastically to fit my own needs for the project; though it is still important to remember that without Shimmer there would likely be no Gleam.
   ```
3. **Omission of `MIT` Notice & Incompatible Relicensing (`Gleam @ 92421398fd`):**
   Root directory listing of `ThatJadenXgamer/Gleam` (`1.21.1-neo` `HEAD`):
   ```text
   .gitignore, README.md, build.gradle, gradle.properties, gradle/, gradlew, gradlew.bat, libs/, settings.gradle, src/
   ```
   `Gleam` contains **no `LICENSE` file**, omits `Copyright (c) 2022 Low-Drag-MC` and the mandatory `MIT` permission notice from all source and resource files, and declares at `README.md:169`:
   ```text
   Gleam (c) 2026 by ThatJadenXgamer (ThatMaidenJaden) is licensed under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0
   ```

### 3.2 Side-by-Side Comparison: `Shimmer` (`shimmer.glsl`) vs. `Gleam` First Code Commit (`ae3265ac9a`, `2026-08-23`)

```glsl
// Low-Drag-MC/Shimmer: Common/src/main/resources/assets/minecraft/shaders/include/shimmer.glsl
struct Light {
    vec4 color;
    vec3 position;
    float radius;
};
layout (std140) uniform Lights {
    Light lights[2048];
};
layout (std140) uniform Env {
    int uvLightCout;
    int nouvLightCout;
    vec3 camPos;
};
vec3 jodieReinhardTonemap(vec3 c){
    float l = dot(c, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));
    vec3 tc = c / (c + 1.0);

    return mix(c / (l + 1.0), tc, tc);
}
```

```glsl
// ThatJadenXgamer/Gleam Commit ae3265ac9acca94f588c865682ed6b6d44820037 (GleamShaderPatcher.java)
struct GleamLightSource {
    vec4 color;
    vec3 position;
    float radius;
};
layout(std140, binding = 10) uniform GleamLight {
    GleamLightSource lights[64];
};
layout(std140, binding = 11) uniform GleamScene {
    int lightCount;
    vec3 cameraPos;
};
vec3 applyTonemap(vec3 color) {
    float lum = dot(color, vec3(0.2126, 0.7152, 0.0722));
    vec3 mapped = color / (color + 1.0);
    return mix(color / (lum + 1.0), mapped, mapped);
}
```

* Commit `ae3265ac9a` (`2026-08-23 20:31:29 +0530`) simultaneously introduced three `public final class` utility classes with `private` empty constructors (`GleamEmitterRegistry`, `GleamLightEngine`, `GleamShaderPatcher`), compared against `0` `private` utility constructors across `303` classes (`34,041` LOC) of `Jadens-Nether-Expansion`.
* Five days later (`ef0597140d`, `2026-08-28 03:38:11 +0530`, `"HEAVILY optimized gleam"`), `GleamLightEngine` was replaced with an OpenGL `4.3` `std430` `GL_SHADER_STORAGE_BUFFER` (`SSBO`) `32x32x32` spatial grid featuring `0xFFFF` twin-`uint16` overflow packing at `currentCount == 127`, `MapMaker().weakKeys()` concurrent section tracking, Rec.709 luminance saturation math, and cubic Hermite smoothstep LOD (`t * t * (3.0f - 2.0f * t)`), containing **`0` Javadoc blocks and `2` single-line comments across `1,988` LOC**.
* In Commit `2bb5dd5` (`2026-09-08 20:42:09 +0530`, **prior to Issue `#1`**), `ThatJadenXgamer` added two separate denials to `README.md` (`line 27`: *"NO generative AI was used; because Gleam is a 'shining' example of how you dont need to use ai"* and `lines 159-161`: *"Q: Is this mod AI-generated? A: As stated earlier, NO."*).

### 3.3 Documented Shader & OpenGL Defects in `Gleam` Issue Tracker

1. **Issue `#7` (`2026-09-15`, open and unanswered): Permanent Freeze on macOS (`OpenGL 4.1` Hardware Ceiling vs. `#version 430 core`):**
   * `Shimmer` used `#version 150` + `GL31` `UBO`s (`2,048` lights) because Apple's macOS OpenGL driver stack terminates at OpenGL `4.1` (`#version 410`) and does not support OpenGL `4.3` (`#version 430` / `GL_SHADER_STORAGE_BUFFER`). `Gleam` rewrites shaders to `#version 430 core` with `std430` SSBOs (`GleamSodiumPatcher.java:7`, `GleamVeilPreProcessor.java:46`), hanging macOS clients at `Gleam: patched vertex shader 'rendertype_solid'`.
2. **Issue `#10` (`2026-10-31`, open and unfixed): Naive `#extension` String Splicing Crashes `Polytone`:**
   * `GleamSodiumPatcher` and `GleamVanillaPatcher` splice `#extension GL_ARB_shader_storage_buffer_object : enable` via raw `source.indexOf("\n", versionIdx)`. When `Polytone` modifies shader headers, OpenGL aborts compilation with `1:87(1): error: #extension directive is not allowed in the middle of a shader`.
3. **Issue `#3` (`2026-09-12`) -> PR `#12` (`aef59ea`, `2026-11-12` by `MikelR1`): `62`-Day Unfixed 2-Line Tint Bug:**
   * `GleamShaderSources.java` overwrote biome block tints for `62` days until external contributor `MikelR1` fixed `2` lines in PR `#12` (`1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)`).
4. **PR `#11` (`4e7b584`, `2026-11-11` by `Zonix-Official`):**
   * `RebuildTaskMixin` and `ChunkBuilderMeshingTaskMixin` used fixed literal vanilla Y-bounds `-64` to `319` instead of querying `getMinBuildHeight()` and `getMaxBuildHeight() - 1`.

